{"school":{"dbn":"24Q005","name":"I.S. 5 - The Walter Crowley Intermediate School","boro":"Queens","district":"24","district_label":"District 24","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1201,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"50-40 JACOBUS STREET, QUEENS, NY 11373","phone":"718-326-2111","website":null,"directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63655","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"At I.S. 5 We Talk Like Scholars, Write Like Experts, Think Like Innovators and Live Like Leaders! Students appreciate that I.S. 5 provides them with a welcoming, affirming and nurturing environment that pairs the development of academic strengths with the deepening of socio-emotional skills to prepare our young people to be dynamic leaders. Relationships and connections are so important to the middle school experience, and we put the physical and emotional safety and wellbeing of our school first! At I.S. 5 we have \u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u009cCommunities\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u009d, each with an assigned assistant principal, dean and school counselor who work with students through all three years. Our I.S. 5 Scholars, Experts, Innovators and Leaders all engage in weekly advisory classes that champion the positive and inspiring 7 Habits of Effective Teens and The Leader in Me as well as embrace our schoolwide commitment to our Core Values: respect, integrity, empathy, accountability and, most importantly, building connection and community with each other. I.S. 5 academics set all students up for the bright and bold futures ahead of them through a unified and rigorous shared curriculum that highlights concepts and ideas that resonate with our students, paired with a range of learning opportunities to address areas of need and enrichment that are essential for success through our new What I Need (WIN) and Strategic Reading Periods (SRP). From hands-on projects that highlight citizenship, voice and contribution, to science investigations, critical thinking and inquiry, to math explorations and application to real world, to literacy spotlights on the lived experiences of our students, we believe at I.S. 5 that our academics and studies stretch well beyond the classroom, preparing our students for high school and beyond. Our current curriculum for the four cores are HMH into Literature, SAVVAS Envisions, Amplify and Passport to Social Studies which are further enriched by World Language Spanish, a full complement of Fine and Performing Arts classes, Computer Science, Civic Leadership, Financial Literacy and Physical Education. We are proud to offer The I.S. 5 Dual Language Program in Spanish (housed in the Community of Scholars) and The I.S. 5 Leadership in STEM Program (housed currently within the Community of Innovators & Leaders), each of which provide another avenue for families and students to join I.S. 5 for their middle school years. We hope you consider being a part of the I.S. 5 school community!","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"M, R to Elmhurst Av","bus":"Q18, Q47, Q53-SBS, Q58, Q59, Q60","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Elmhurst","latitude":40.737181,"longitude":-73.887907,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.926],"st":["ok"],"n":[773.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.958,0.962,0.924,0.916,0.927,0.927,0.925],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[1857.0,1819.0,1673.0,1695.0,1497.0,1394.0,1298.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.912]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.924],"st":["ok"],"n":[1667.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.926,0.917,0.911,0.895,0.909,0.772,0.7